# A first Dynamic stroke on a dense Part with a big brush (a remeshed head, Detail 23): it coarsens the surface under the
# brush every dab, in clusters all over the brush's disc, and used to send the whole Part to the GPU every frame (and,
# in a big scene, rebuild its coarse levels each time): the stroke stalled for seconds. The stroke's remeshed clusters go
# up as patches, and the Part is sent whole once at most (at the release, when the patches outnumber a fresh layout's).
run new_bench_sphere millions=0.5
wait 0.5
expect_value triangles > 400000
run dyntopo enabled=true detail=23 freeze_levels=true
click "Clay Block##brush.clayblock"
brush_size 120
remember triangles before
remember part_full_uploads uploads
stroke 0.35 0.4 0.6 0.5
wait 0.3
expect_value triangles < $before
expect_value part_full_uploads <= $uploads+2
expect_value render_patch_errors == 0
stroke 0.4 0.6 0.65 0.55
wait 0.3
expect_value part_full_uploads <= $uploads+4
expect_value render_patch_errors == 0
shot first_stroke
